r/id #uuid "c0c69163-b00f-58d2-9ead-f4267caae5a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fa5cf22-9fbc-5faa-a78b-7a79de5312d4" :answer/id #uuid "9fa5cf22-9fbc-5faa-a78b-7a79de5312d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae8713d7-4691-5e08-870e-3fc604e3a336" :question/id #uuid "ae8713d7-4691-5e08-870e-3fc604e3a336" :question/math-academy-id "q-250599" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=5(x+1)^{2}+8.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex.\n\n- Since $h=-1$ and $k=8,$ the vertex is $(-1,8).$\n\n- Since $a=5>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $[8,\\infty ),$ i.e. $8\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/7f/7ff6f49b63c4ad55324bbb406558781c9f3e5af3a98d34b285c65f88746bddab.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-14dd9f6b-b90d-536d-a13a-6a8b2fd1a148" "answer-field-88ae973c-62f9-56f2-a4a1-2371757dfc39" "answer-field-2d759167-da63-50ff-b449-46e9207401d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-14dd9f6b-b90d-536d-a13a-6a8b2fd1a148" :answer-field/id #uuid "14dd9f6b-b90d-536d-a13a-6a8b2fd1a148" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b0550c3e-d926-5110-81d5-70fdbb769ee0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b0550c3e-d926-5110-81d5-70fdbb769ee0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0550c3e-d926-5110-81d5-70fdbb769ee0" :answer/id #uuid "b0550c3e-d926-5110-81d5-70fdbb769ee0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-88ae973c-62f9-56f2-a4a1-2371757dfc39" :answer-field/id #uuid "88ae973c-62f9-56f2-a4a1-2371757dfc39" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3b03abe2-8172-576d-97e4-0f4f7c428220" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b03abe2-8172-576d-97e4-0f4f7c428220"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b03abe2-8172-576d-97e4-0f4f7c428220" :answer/id #uuid "3b03abe2-8172-576d-97e4-0f4f7c428220" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2d759167-da63-50ff-b449-46e9207401d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d759167-da63-50ff-b449-46e9207401d6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2cf36b9c-d2df-5984-9e40-401bf59336ca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2cf36b9c-d2df-5984-9e40-401bf59336ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cf36b9c-d2df-5984-9e40-401bf59336ca" :answer/id #uuid "2cf36b9c-d2df-5984-9e40-401bf59336ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124866 :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)={(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-\\frac{5}{6}$ and $k=-\\frac{1}{2},$ the vertex is $(-\\frac{5}{6},-\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\n- Since $a=1>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $[-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty ).$ \n\n![](images/54/54e0b0ea5dd498a36fc854781dc5120ce1de9bee0c333eecc6d895ce09b72424.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121796 :answer-field/correct "answer-a19b54fd-b859-58ec-9f48-c6622db47056" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b8a8d8b1-1116-562c-9eac-92b96751313a" "answer-4e47ff5f-6b08-5d07-a62a-c241fb59bdf0" "answer-25995585-8181-58ec-9ca2-df6919080cd3" "answer-a19b54fd-b859-58ec-9f48-c6622db47056" "answer-e364e522-0636-5c3f-b534-a21b5528a7bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8a8d8b1-1116-562c-9eac-92b96751313a" :answer/id #uuid "b8a8d8b1-1116-562c-9eac-92b96751313a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e47ff5f-6b08-5d07-a62a-c241fb59bdf0" :answer/id #uuid "4e47ff5f-6b08-5d07-a62a-c241fb59bdf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-\\frac{1}{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25995585-8181-58ec-9ca2-df6919080cd3" :answer/id #uuid "25995585-8181-58ec-9ca2-df6919080cd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{6}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a19b54fd-b859-58ec-9f48-c6622db47056" :answer/id #uuid "a19b54fd-b859-58ec-9f48-c6622db47056" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e364e522-0636-5c3f-b534-a21b5528a7bf" :answer/id #uuid "e364e522-0636-5c3f-b534-a21b5528a7bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-\\frac{5}{6},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a24bba0b-6082-5434-98a9-2578424db732" :question/id #uuid "a24bba0b-6082-5434-98a9-2578424db732" :question/math-academy-id "q-106279" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}(x-8)^{2}-18?$" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=8$ and $k=-18,$ the vertex is $(8,-18).$\n\n- Since $a=\\frac{1}{2}>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $[-18,\\infty ).$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/a1/a115822cf26b79f0b25ed5493f5951c71c02c6ef5a4d576d101b4bc580d5da9f.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c7d9884e-0ead-53ae-8a5b-cde350ebf44a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c7d9884e-0ead-53ae-8a5b-cde350ebf44a" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7d9884e-0ead-53ae-8a5b-cde350ebf44a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3a31478e-4c7c-5de1-8fad-3638ee4a8f27" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3a31478e-4c7c-5de1-8fad-3638ee4a8f27" "answer-8a2b0a49-4051-52d2-805a-b79331b4101a" "answer-d9c83282-9161-5639-be3f-86063ce871cd" "answer-8d0e44e7-7189-5fcd-aa1a-51e9e932ef54" "answer-20198d03-e820-5496-9e93-29432b8ff469"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a31478e-4c7c-5de1-8fad-3638ee4a8f27" :answer/id #uuid "3a31478e-4c7c-5de1-8fad-3638ee4a8f27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-18,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a2b0a49-4051-52d2-805a-b79331b4101a" :answer/id #uuid "8a2b0a49-4051-52d2-805a-b79331b4101a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-8,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9c83282-9161-5639-be3f-86063ce871cd" :answer/id #uuid "d9c83282-9161-5639-be3f-86063ce871cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-9,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d0e44e7-7189-5fcd-aa1a-51e9e932ef54" :answer/id #uuid "8d0e44e7-7189-5fcd-aa1a-51e9e932ef54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[4,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20198d03-e820-5496-9e93-29432b8ff469" :answer/id #uuid "20198d03-e820-5496-9e93-29432b8ff469" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[8,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2002fa84-a05e-5e54-ad18-933be8248d10" :question/id #uuid "2002fa84-a05e-5e54-ad18-933be8248d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-250607" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-3(x+5)^{2}+7.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)\\le $\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-5$ and $k=7,$ the vertex is $(-5,7).$\n\n- Since $a=-3<0,$ the parabola opens downwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens downwards, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $(-\\infty ,7],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 7.$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/25/252a3c0475f838b1835f2da9c3c818a938c916b781c5abaa1f12ed09c52c56f6.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-56f50417-a8db-5569-b297-00307ac7e3ed" "answer-field-e90fc8d9-ab85-53eb-b3c7-0a25c8c47225" "answer-field-fa3565a8-730f-5135-b58e-5e5914abff83"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-56f50417-a8db-5569-b297-00307ac7e3ed" :answer-field/id #uuid "56f50417-a8db-5569-b297-00307ac7e3ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-80ef7f3f-43e2-5afc-b357-efcbd63dcaec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-80ef7f3f-43e2-5afc-b357-efcbd63dcaec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80ef7f3f-43e2-5afc-b357-efcbd63dcaec" :answer/id #uuid "80ef7f3f-43e2-5afc-b357-efcbd63dcaec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e90fc8d9-ab85-53eb-b3c7-0a25c8c47225" :answer-field/id #uuid "e90fc8d9-ab85-53eb-b3c7-0a25c8c47225" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f0a5d71b-22b4-5f8a-b763-aa7e35f62c9f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0a5d71b-22b4-5f8a-b763-aa7e35f62c9f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0a5d71b-22b4-5f8a-b763-aa7e35f62c9f" :answer/id #uuid "f0a5d71b-22b4-5f8a-b763-aa7e35f62c9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fa3565a8-730f-5135-b58e-5e5914abff83" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa3565a8-730f-5135-b58e-5e5914abff83" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e9317a34-9fc1-5c7d-a546-fec08a118649" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e9317a34-9fc1-5c7d-a546-fec08a118649"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9317a34-9fc1-5c7d-a546-fec08a118649" :answer/id #uuid "e9317a34-9fc1-5c7d-a546-fec08a118649" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5e73f5fc-13ec-5727-bb90-2579fb0880d6" :question/id #uuid "5e73f5fc-13ec-5727-bb90-2579fb0880d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-250633" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+8x+11.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=2>0,$ $b=8,$ and $c=11.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{8}{2\\cdot 2}=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=-2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{2}+8x+11 \\\\  & =2(-2)^{2}+8(-2)+11 \\\\  & =8-16+11 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-2,3),$ and the range of the function is $[3,\\infty ),$ i.e. $3\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\n![](images/3a/3a87830f59bf840ac8ab0d761ab7319b53fc804bc9d925e92850313d5d5a7a52.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2ea59e43-3e9e-551b-b8f4-d4b59960c0d1" "answer-field-3cb67adb-362a-502d-ba97-5bf0f0b88ad1" "answer-field-09ce1543-bab3-5287-8403-e2b7bf000729"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2ea59e43-3e9e-551b-b8f4-d4b59960c0d1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ea59e43-3e9e-551b-b8f4-d4b59960c0d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3b8db516-3ec3-52ed-bcd3-204a1eac8e73" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b8db516-3ec3-52ed-bcd3-204a1eac8e73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b8db516-3ec3-52ed-bcd3-204a1eac8e73" :answer/id #uuid "3b8db516-3ec3-52ed-bcd3-204a1eac8e73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3cb67adb-362a-502d-ba97-5bf0f0b88ad1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3cb67adb-362a-502d-ba97-5bf0f0b88ad1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-17a85056-0a28-50b2-a9dc-d58df89de9a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-17a85056-0a28-50b2-a9dc-d58df89de9a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17a85056-0a28-50b2-a9dc-d58df89de9a3" :answer/id #uuid "17a85056-0a28-50b2-a9dc-d58df89de9a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-09ce1543-bab3-5287-8403-e2b7bf000729" :answer-field/id #uuid "09ce1543-bab3-5287-8403-e2b7bf000729" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c9125bed-e59b-5820-bb19-1b272efd5b76" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c9125bed-e59b-5820-bb19-1b272efd5b76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9125bed-e59b-5820-bb19-1b272efd5b76" :answer/id #uuid "c9125bed-e59b-5820-bb19-1b272efd5b76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-16afc9a4-390c-580b-b4f5-9f8ca64be1a7" :question/id #uuid "16afc9a4-390c-580b-b4f5-9f8ca64be1a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-154270" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x+5?$" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=3>0,$ $b=-6,$ and $c=5.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{(-6)}{2\\cdot 3}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=1$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3{x}^{2}-6x+5 \\\\  & =3(1)^{2}-6(1)+5 \\\\  & =3-6+5 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(1,2),$ and the range of the function is $[2,\\infty ).$\n\n![](images/91/915c1435f78f8a5f85a104b40d9ee83c54c218f8e81b6ea7fc051367055fc624.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fc73fd49-ad93-51ca-81e7-7caa58db6c5f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fc73fd49-ad93-51ca-81e7-7caa58db6c5f" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc73fd49-ad93-51ca-81e7-7caa58db6c5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a1fd0b4a-458f-56d9-a72b-4fcec594a2bf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d93ed979-a31a-5d1a-a93c-591126feb602" "answer-6e2f1db6-cccc-5d24-9a2d-142ff1ee9a9c" "answer-9d4e9999-7fc5-563b-b703-5c6492439ade" "answer-0541d29e-1a3d-5725-a3e8-30e78b5ddec7" "answer-a1fd0b4a-458f-56d9-a72b-4fcec594a2bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d93ed979-a31a-5d1a-a93c-591126feb602" :answer/id #uuid "d93ed979-a31a-5d1a-a93c-591126feb602" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-2]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e2f1db6-cccc-5d24-9a2d-142ff1ee9a9c" :answer/id #uuid "6e2f1db6-cccc-5d24-9a2d-142ff1ee9a9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d4e9999-7fc5-563b-b703-5c6492439ade" :answer/id #uuid "9d4e9999-7fc5-563b-b703-5c6492439ade" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0541d29e-1a3d-5725-a3e8-30e78b5ddec7" :answer/id #uuid "0541d29e-1a3d-5725-a3e8-30e78b5ddec7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1fd0b4a-458f-56d9-a72b-4fcec594a2bf" :answer/id #uuid "a1fd0b4a-458f-56d9-a72b-4fcec594a2bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-89ea5a4a-e490-551f-988c-728a0c124eab" :question/id #uuid "89ea5a4a-e490-551f-988c-728a0c124eab" :question/math-academy-id "q-250639" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+4x+1.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=-1<0,$ $b=4,$ and $c=1.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{4}{2\\cdot (-1)}=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{2}+4x+1 \\\\  & =-(2)^{2}+4(2)+1 \\\\  & =-4+8+1 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(2,5),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,5],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 5.$\n\n![](images/ce/ce52355662b526af83614a6c4cbe6e7f2d7f07d379b2636d14e094d47e0e0da6.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8e23828e-dbe8-55aa-ba5d-1021ce14ba4b" "answer-field-788caaeb-874f-5a58-a638-27770e22a12b" "answer-field-c1c47709-4fb4-5410-8bb2-077d0d2f6c96"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8e23828e-dbe8-55aa-ba5d-1021ce14ba4b" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e23828e-dbe8-55aa-ba5d-1021ce14ba4b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-560383cf-7bf3-5f2c-8cdd-a33f83f8439c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-560383cf-7bf3-5f2c-8cdd-a33f83f8439c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-560383cf-7bf3-5f2c-8cdd-a33f83f8439c" :answer/id #uuid "560383cf-7bf3-5f2c-8cdd-a33f83f8439c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-788caaeb-874f-5a58-a638-27770e22a12b" :answer-field/id #uuid "788caaeb-874f-5a58-a638-27770e22a12b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6431dec3-2744-5c91-9888-35fb8d486a49" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6431dec3-2744-5c91-9888-35fb8d486a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6431dec3-2744-5c91-9888-35fb8d486a49" :answer/id #uuid "6431dec3-2744-5c91-9888-35fb8d486a49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c1c47709-4fb4-5410-8bb2-077d0d2f6c96" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1c47709-4fb4-5410-8bb2-077d0d2f6c96" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-35735545-6764-5af4-8b30-c44340961668" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35735545-6764-5af4-8b30-c44340961668"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35735545-6764-5af4-8b30-c44340961668" :answer/id #uuid "35735545-6764-5af4-8b30-c44340961668" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125237 :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-4x+5?$" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=2>0,$ $b=-4,$ and $c=5.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{(-4)}{2\\cdot 2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=1$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{2}-4x+5 \\\\  & =2(1)^{2}-4(1)+5 \\\\  & =2-4+5 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(1,3),$ and the range of the function is $[3,\\infty ).$\n\n![](images/a8/a8fc15df2b24054485bb07330f40919ebf13cb9969073a733b9426a28dab20b5.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124022 :answer-field/correct "answer-e6a97956-8fdf-547f-bcc6-039d7a0099a2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81c5bbf2-cb3f-5027-93c7-adfd59d8054d" "answer-ba14fcfa-ffa6-571d-88a3-f4da05a8b41d" "answer-abd657a4-c200-5733-9a0a-52aadbe8c41c" "answer-e6a97956-8fdf-547f-bcc6-039d7a0099a2" "answer-f39445c2-f0a2-5251-85ea-f5894b6372ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81c5bbf2-cb3f-5027-93c7-adfd59d8054d" :answer/id #uuid "81c5bbf2-cb3f-5027-93c7-adfd59d8054d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba14fcfa-ffa6-571d-88a3-f4da05a8b41d" :answer/id #uuid "ba14fcfa-ffa6-571d-88a3-f4da05a8b41d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,5]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abd657a4-c200-5733-9a0a-52aadbe8c41c" :answer/id #uuid "abd657a4-c200-5733-9a0a-52aadbe8c41c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6a97956-8fdf-547f-bcc6-039d7a0099a2" :answer/id #uuid "e6a97956-8fdf-547f-bcc6-039d7a0099a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f39445c2-f0a2-5251-85ea-f5894b6372ed" :answer/id #uuid "f39445c2-f0a2-5251-85ea-f5894b6372ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[5,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-da80a3c6-7cc5-5c7d-84d3-2b9e185bcdef" :question/id #uuid "da80a3c6-7cc5-5c7d-84d3-2b9e185bcdef" :question/math-academy-id "q-90989" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)(x+6)?$" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=\\frac{1}{2}>0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-6,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{2+(-6)}{2}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=-2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)(x+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-2-2)(-2+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-2,-8),$ and the range of the function is $[-8,\\infty ).$\n\n![](images/ba/bac4e1a79c32d61d6bc348564b2d791a06d19b0126c49af0689dd821d5063b4e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bd54b7e3-2076-5436-90fa-bb06bb950450"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bd54b7e3-2076-5436-90fa-bb06bb950450" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd54b7e3-2076-5436-90fa-bb06bb950450" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fcb79e4a-a3fc-58ba-8a56-dedf17d975a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-70c6a83b-dcfd-5c3d-bc2b-e9915f5cdd8f" "answer-ac845ab8-38a7-5044-9f5b-4864e79bb7a7" "answer-e0faab00-b0a3-584d-8c56-e28428306bab" "answer-fcb79e4a-a3fc-58ba-8a56-dedf17d975a8" "answer-b852e5bc-7670-5fa0-842e-aa867be2b474"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70c6a83b-dcfd-5c3d-bc2b-e9915f5cdd8f" :answer/id #uuid "70c6a83b-dcfd-5c3d-bc2b-e9915f5cdd8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-8]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac845ab8-38a7-5044-9f5b-4864e79bb7a7" :answer/id #uuid "ac845ab8-38a7-5044-9f5b-4864e79bb7a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,6]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0faab00-b0a3-584d-8c56-e28428306bab" :answer/id #uuid "e0faab00-b0a3-584d-8c56-e28428306bab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcb79e4a-a3fc-58ba-8a56-dedf17d975a8" :answer/id #uuid "fcb79e4a-a3fc-58ba-8a56-dedf17d975a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-8,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b852e5bc-7670-5fa0-842e-aa867be2b474" :answer/id #uuid "b852e5bc-7670-5fa0-842e-aa867be2b474" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[6,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8a31f28b-9e61-5b12-8422-c1bd2c17fb23" :question/id #uuid "8a31f28b-9e61-5b12-8422-c1bd2c17fb23" :question/math-academy-id "q-250644" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=(x-2)(x-8).$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)<$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=1>0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=8,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{2+8}{2}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=5$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(x-2)(x-8) \\\\  & =(5-2)(5-8) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(5,-9),$ and the range of the function is $[-9,\\infty ),$ i.e. $-9\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\n![](images/84/84c22aee72ebd52e3dab84a72ad1d402813c3a38794c653cd4cb0e31bfef3836.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-453c5296-23d3-57ab-bead-b0c23a1b99d7" "answer-field-cf3e671d-1011-5362-908e-3f28855f4af3" "answer-field-7323c510-56c5-5c7a-8032-b64a15edc529"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-453c5296-23d3-57ab-bead-b0c23a1b99d7" :answer-field/id #uuid "453c5296-23d3-57ab-bead-b0c23a1b99d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-78afb764-e323-511a-a2f2-0a8264faacfd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78afb764-e323-511a-a2f2-0a8264faacfd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78afb764-e323-511a-a2f2-0a8264faacfd" :answer/id #uuid "78afb764-e323-511a-a2f2-0a8264faacfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cf3e671d-1011-5362-908e-3f28855f4af3" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf3e671d-1011-5362-908e-3f28855f4af3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6a2fff73-ed51-5034-b645-c0efebc9c710" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6a2fff73-ed51-5034-b645-c0efebc9c710"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a2fff73-ed51-5034-b645-c0efebc9c710" :answer/id #uuid "6a2fff73-ed51-5034-b645-c0efebc9c710" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7323c510-56c5-5c7a-8032-b64a15edc529" :answer-field/id #uuid "7323c510-56c5-5c7a-8032-b64a15edc529" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6c978228-4f12-5690-9c85-cedfcd98d83e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6c978228-4f12-5690-9c85-cedfcd98d83e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c978228-4f12-5690-9c85-cedfcd98d83e" :answer/id #uuid "6c978228-4f12-5690-9c85-cedfcd98d83e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fe465ece-00d7-560c-ae8f-64c0313299b0" :question/id #uuid "fe465ece-00d7-560c-ae8f-64c0313299b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-250645" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{5}(x+9)(x-1).$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=\\frac{1}{5}>0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-9$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-9+1}{2}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=-4$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{5}(x+9)(x-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(-4+9)(-4-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-4,-5),$ and the range of the function is $[-5,\\infty ),$ i.e. $-5\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\n![](images/97/97c587abebf09ff27a805db3b32b3c5f26b5d51baaf7f6827618e01ccdd53642.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61e49312-09ef-5c75-8f30-c37d021b2a52" "answer-field-00a2dd0c-399e-5d39-b0f4-c489761a9a1d" "answer-field-7ca70ad5-e447-592a-96e6-edc3042e22c9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61e49312-09ef-5c75-8f30-c37d021b2a52" :answer-field/id #uuid "61e49312-09ef-5c75-8f30-c37d021b2a52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7870eb48-797a-5ba2-9a14-64ab4a64026e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7870eb48-797a-5ba2-9a14-64ab4a64026e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7870eb48-797a-5ba2-9a14-64ab4a64026e" :answer/id #uuid "7870eb48-797a-